[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3094527897","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108796#issuecomment-3094527897","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108796","id":3094527897,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64cr-Z","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-20T13:43:45Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T13:43:45Z","body":"The crash is not reproducible on API level >= 28. It seems Android handles clipboard access differently on newer versions.\r\n\r\nSince this solution blocks the thread, do we want to restrict it only to API <= 27 and continue calling the method directly on newer versions?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3094527897/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3099867526","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108796#issuecomment-3099867526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108796","id":3099867526,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64xDmG","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-21T23:22:53Z","updated_at":"2025-07-21T23:22:53Z","body":"> Let's use a [`FutureTask`](https://developer.android.com/reference/java/util/concurrent/FutureTask) instead. For api <= 27, you can submit the `FutureTask` to the `mainExecutor`. For api > 27, you can just call `FutureTask#run()` directly.\r\n\r\nQuick clarification; you should create persistent `Callable` fields to wrap the logic for each method:\r\n- on api > 27, you call the `Callable` directly and return their result (this way we're not allocated new objects for each method call)\r\n- on api <= 27, you wrap the `Callable` in a `FutureTask` and submit it to the `mainExecutor`. We're allocating new `FutureTask` objects on each invocation, but there's no other options.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3099867526/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3101438549","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108796#issuecomment-3101438549","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108796","id":3101438549,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc643DJV","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-22T07:32:25Z","updated_at":"2025-07-22T07:59:54Z","body":"@m4gr3d Does this looks good now?\r\n\r\nI kept `setClipboard()` to always run on the UI thread across all Android versions. Since it doesn't return a value, there's no need to block the call on older versions, and running on UI thread doesn't cause any issues on newer ones either.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3101438549/reactions","total_count":1,